  "summary_text": "Kyle, yesterday's results need to be read through the Independence Day lens. Port Washington posted $3,099 (up 12% vs last Monday), but that's meaningless without context\u2014we're two days out from a holiday that typically crushes Monday revenue by 50%. The real story is capacity and productivity. Port ran 5 groomers and generated $511 per groomer-day, slightly under the 30-day baseline of $518, which is fine. What matters more: core grooming revenue jumped 19% week-over-week despite flat appointment count, suggesting solid upsell discipline. However, add-on attach fell from 56% to 48%, and retail dropped 12%\u2014both operational signals worth your attention on the front-of-house. MTD Port is down 13% absolute, but DOW-adjusted expectation pulls that gap to -11.3%, so the calendar mix is real but we're still underrunning slightly. The bright spot: your 12+ week visit-gap bucket is shrinking (15.5% to 13.3%), a leading indicator that retention is improving.\n\nHicksville is the concern. Yesterday one groomer produced $570 against a 30-day baseline of $403\u2014excellent productivity from Julia, but the store itself is structurally undersized. You had only 1 groomer scheduled on a Monday post-holiday; that's not Julia's problem, it's a capacity planning problem. Retail cratered 65% (8 vs 17 transactions), which tracks with capacity\u2014fewer customers in the door means fewer retail touches. MTD Hicksville is only 4% down on revenue and actually beating DOW-adjusted expectations by 11.6%, so operationally it's flat. But the leading indicator is red: your 12+ week bucket is growing 2.4 points to 12.6%, meaning customers are stretching out their visits. This is stealth churn.\n\nThe pattern: Port Washington is humming (50% YoY growth), while Hicksville needs groomer density. You have 496 customers in Port's lapse pool ($316k annual value) and 84 in Hicksville's ($61k). Prioritize reactivation at Port\u2014you have the capacity to absorb them.\n\n**Capacity & coverage: Today 6 groomers Port + 1 groomer Hicksville (7 total) with 0 bather hours; tomorrow 6 + 1 with 7 bather hours Port-side; next 7 days 34 groomer-days Port and 5 Hicksville (39 total), 43 bather hours Port-only.**"
